  "findings": [
    "Baseline represents six arm revolute DOFs and one independently driven gripper DOF with equal-travel opposed prismatic jaws. Seven motor actuators must not become seven serial arm joints.",
    "All mesh vertices are assembly-coordinate millimetres. At q=0 every link visual has CAD-to-base transform identity rotation and [0,-0.0257,0] m translation. CAD +Y is up. Rotate complete assembly +90 degrees around X for conventional Z-up.",
    "J2-J3 and J3-J4 baseline joint-center lengths are both 190 mm; J3-J4 is vector [-174,76.315136,0] mm because CAD zero is bent.",
    "All arm effort=10 Nm, velocity=5 rad/s and angular limits are inherited unverified; do not use as RS00 specifications.",
    "All masses/inertias are unverified designer estimates. Baseline total mass 3.38 kg; fixed wrist plus two jaws sums 0.4 kg. Jaw masses derived by partitioning uniform mesh density 1246.9258626 kg/m3, not measured material mass.",
    "Hidden collision loop meshes 46 and 47 remain even though their visuals were removed. Internal drive meshes 23,24,25,28,29,30,35,36,37,42 omitted from visuals and collisions; their inertia remains lumped in link_007.",
    "Gripper full gap = 2 * gripper_left_joint; range 0..104.825 mm gap and 0..52.4125 mm per-jaw travel. Mimic multiplier +1 is correct because jaw axes already oppose. Some simulators ignore URDF mimic.",
    "J7 motor-to-gap preview mapping uses closed encoder +0.00671320668 rad and commanded-open -2.07898420691 rad. Full-open physical gap and intermediate nonlinearity are explicitly unverified. Do not equate J7 radians with the prismatic coordinate.",
    "No armature, rotor reflected inertia, friction, damping, actuator dynamics or transmission model exists in baseline. No self-collision exclusions; triangle meshes are reused as collision meshes.",
    "Baseline omits CAD part_003 with purpose and ownership unverified.",
    "Reuse link_005 onward and joints link_006_joint/link_007_joint/gripper joints/grasp_center structurally if identical J4-J7 geometry is confirmed. Keep those meshes and local transforms together. Update J4 upstream origin using new CAD alignment, not only scalar link-length changes.",
    "Build new proximal link inertia from new geometry and RS00 motor assignment; do not retain RS02-era link_002/link_003/link_004 physical parameters. Distal reused inertia remains provisional until weighed."
  ],
